2. vLLM (Apache License 2.0), https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm
   The proxy reproduces documented behaviour of vLLM 0.19.1: the chat template content
   format detection, the OpenAI message preprocessing, the gemma4 reasoning and tool-call
   parsers, the context-length validation messages and the thinking-token-budget logits
   processor. At runtime the kit loads vLLM's own gemma4 argument parser from a file the
   user supplies (vllm/tool_parsers/gemma4_tool_parser.py); that file is not distributed
   here. The built-in fallback parser is an independent implementation of the same format.

3. Gemma 4 chat template (Apache License 2.0, per the google/gemma-4-31B-it model repository)
   Not distributed here. The proxy reads chat_template.jinja from a path the user supplies.
   The test fixture tests/fixtures/mini_chat_template.jinja is a small hand-written template
   that is modelled on the official template's turn format, for unit tests only.

4. SWE-Lego error masking (a training rule; no code or data from that work is included)
   Tao, C., Chen, J., Jiang, Y., et al. "SWE-Lego: Pushing the Limits of Supervised Fine-tuning for Software
   Issue Resolving", arXiv:2601.01426, 2026.
   g4kit-curate's tool-error rule and g4kit-render-distill --mask-error-turns tool adapt the error masking of
   its fine-tuning procedure: no loss on a turn whose tool call failed because of the call itself (file-tool
   errors, shell invocation errors, pytest usage errors), while failing tests and reproduction runs stay trained.

5. LoRA Without Regret (a parametrization; no code is included)
   Schulman, J. and Thinking Machines Lab, "LoRA Without Regret", Sep 29, 2025,
   https://thinkingmachines.ai/blog/lora/.
   examples/tpu uses its LoRA parametrization (alpha 32 with scale alpha / r, A initialized uniformly with
   scale 1/sqrt(d_in), B at zero) and its learning-rate guidance for the sweep.

6. Tunix and Qwix (Apache License 2.0), https://github.com/google/tunix and https://github.com/google/qwix
   examples/tpu installs both inside the Kaggle kernel from its pinned lock file and maps their LoRA parameter
   layouts to PEFT's; no code from them is included here.
